.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
This "help" flag causes the program to print out a description
of its operation and then exit immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
The \fB\-\-verbose\fP option causes \fBmbimagecorrect\fP to print out status messages.
.TP
.B \-\-input=\fIimagefile\fP
.br
Sets the filename of the input image to be corrected.
.TP
.B \-\-output=\fIimagefile\fP
.br
Sets the filename of the output, corrected image.
.TP
.B \-\-histogram\-equalization
.br
Selects the histogram equalization correction mode: the Y (luminance) channel
of the image (converted to YCrCb color space) is histogram equalized, and the
result is converted back to BGR.
.TP
.B \-\-gamma\-correction=\fIgamma\fP
.br
Selects the gamma correction mode and sets the gamma exponent used to build the
correction lookup table applied to each of the BGR channels. The default gamma
value is 0.5.
.TP
.B \-\-clahe\-correction
.br
Selects the CLAHE (Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization)
correction mode: the image is converted to Lab color space, CLAHE is applied
to the L (lightness) channel with a clip limit of 4, and the result is
converted back to BGR. This is the default correction mode if no other
correction mode option is specified.
.TP
.B \-\-lightness\-correction=\fIfactor\fP
.br
Selects the simple lightness correction mode and sets the multiplicative
\fIfactor\fP applied to the Y (luminance) channel of the image (converted to
YCrCb color space) before converting back to BGR. The default factor is 1.0.

